  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 2004, a Navy fighter pilot named David Fravor reported that an unidentified object near the aircraft carrier USS Nimitz, off San Diego, dropped from 80,000 feet to sea level almost instantly. The skeptic Michael Shermer brings this up when he debates Michels, and he sets Fravor's account against a calculation by the scientist Avi Loeb that he cites as weighing against it. Shermer does not explain the details of the calculation, but he uses it to question whether such a drop could really have happened as Fravor describes."
